# Event AI Continuity

- Before Event AI work, read `.agents/plans/event-ai-agent-roadmap.md`, `event-ai-agent-execution.md`, and `event-ai-agent-decisions.md`.
- The execution file is the source of current phase, checkpoint, tests, blockers, and next action.
- Work in the smallest independently testable slice; avoid mixing phases in one unverified change.
- Update the checkpoint before stopping, handing off, switching tasks, or when quota/context is at risk.
- Record changed files, migrations, commands, test results, assumptions, unresolved risks, and the exact resume action.
- Mark unverified work explicitly; never let a new agent infer that partial work is complete.
- Add architecture/product choices to the append-only decision log; supersede decisions instead of deleting history.
- Preserve user changes and inspect the dirty worktree before editing.
- Never commit Event AI changes without explicit user authorization.
- A replacement agent must validate the checkpoint against `git status` and the referenced files before continuing.
